description:
Design a clock divider that generates a reduced frequency output clock, clk_out, from an input clock, clk_in. The output clock's frequency is determined by the divide_factor input, which specifies how many input clock cycles are needed to toggle the output. The module includes a 32-bit counter that increments on each rising edge of clk_in and toggles clk_out when the counter reaches the value of divide_factor minus one. Additionally, it features an optional delay before the output clock initializes to LOW, allowing for flexible timing adjustments in applications requiring clock signal management or synchronization.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input [31:0] divide_factor,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input [31:0] divide_factor,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter clk_period = 10; // in nanoseconds
parameter delay_cycles = 0;

reg [31:0] counter = 0;

always @(posedge clk_in) begin
  if (counter == divide_factor - 1) begin
    counter <= 0;
    clk_out <= ~clk_out;
  end else begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
  end
end

initial begin
  #delay_cycles;
  clk_out <= 0;
end

endmodule

