description:
Design a watchdog timer that monitors system activity. The module counts clock cycles and resets when the reset signal is active. If the counter exceeds a predefined timeout period, denoted by parameter 't', the output signal 'wdt' goes high, indicating a timeout has occurred. This functionality is crucial for ensuring system reliability by detecting unresponsive conditions.
module top_module(
  input clk, rst,
  output wdt
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk, rst,
  output wdt
);parameter t = 10; // timeout period in clock cycles

  reg [31:0] counter;

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (rst) begin
      counter <= 0;
    end
    else begin
      counter <= counter + 1;
    end
  end

  assign wdt = (counter >= t) ? 1'b1 : 1'b0;

endmodule

