description:
Design a one-second countdown timer that operates on a 60 Hz clock signal. The module features a synchronous reset and an enable signal. When reset is low, the timer initializes the count to 60. With the enable signal active, the counter decrements the count on every clock pulse until it reaches zero, at which point it generates a one-second pulse on the output `one_sec`. When the count is zero, it resets back to 60.
module top_module(
    input clk60, reset, enable,
    output one_sec
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk60, reset, enable,
    output one_sec
);reg [5:0] count;
    always @(posedge clk60)
    begin
        if (!reset)
            count <= 6'd60;
        else if (enable)
        begin
            if (count == 6'd0)
                count <= 6'd60;
            else
                count <= count - 1'b1;
        end
    end
    assign one_sec = (count == 6'd0) ? 1 : 0;endmodule

